{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is a 3/4 overhead view at a 40-degree angle, centering two simple matte ceramic plates on an aged, weathered oak kitchen table. The main plate in the foreground is in sharp focus, while the second plate sits slightly blurred in the background, representing a meal for two. Each plate holds several square, bite-sized woven whole-wheat crackers, each topped with a single, crisp round of bright green English cucumber and a generous spoonful of roughly chopped pink shrimp mixed with specks of fresh, vibrant green dill, a light glistening of olive oil, and coarse black pepper. There are NO whole shrimp, only bite-sized pink pieces. A shallow depth of field creates a soft natural bokeh on the background. Soft natural side lighting from a window on the left casts subtle, gentle shadows and highlights the pearly, moist texture of the shrimp and the crispness of the cucumber. Props include a small, rumpled linen napkin pushed to the side, a few loose crumbs of woven cracker, and a squeezed lemon half on the wood surface, showing evidence of preparation. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures an authentic, warm, and lived-in moment of a home-cooked lunch. Slight natural imperfections include an asymmetric arrangement of the crackers, a stray piece of dill on the plate rim, and a tiny oil droplet on the wood. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces. The image is indistinguishable from professional editorial cookbook photography."
}
